Quiz Answers: Introduction to Kubernetes and OpenShift
1. What is the installed version for the OpenShift cluster?
✅ Correct Answer:
C — 4.18.6
The lab environment for DO180 4.18 runs OpenShift 4.18.6.
________________________________________
2. Which three severity types are available for the alerts in the cluster?
✅ Correct Answers:
•	A — Warning
•	C — Info
•	E — Critical
These are the standard alert severity levels used in OpenShift monitoring.
❌ Incorrect:
•	Firing → alert state, not severity
•	Urgent → not used
•	Oops → not real
________________________________________
3. Which three labels are on the thanos-querier route in the openshift-monitoring namespace?
✅ Correct Answers:
•	A — app.kubernetes.io/component=query-layer
•	B — app.kubernetes.io/instance=thanos-querier
•	D — app.kubernetes.io/version=0.36.1
❌ Incorrect:
•	app.kubernetes.io/part-of=openshift-storage → wrong component
________________________________________
4. Which two objects are listed as the StorageClasses objects for the cluster?
✅ Correct Answers:
•	D — local-volume
•	E — lvms-vg1
These are typical storage classes created by the LVM Storage operator in the DO180 lab.
________________________________________
5. When All Projects is selected, which three operators are installed in the cluster?
✅ Correct Answers:
•	B — MetalLB Operator
•	D — LVM Storage
•	E — Package Server
❌ Incorrect:
•	MongoDB Operator → not installed by default
•	Red Hat Fuse → not part of base cluster operators

